---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy and processing — Secure Pride"
  description="Where scanner text goes, what the application logs, and which hosting details remain unverified."
  canonicalUrl="https://securepride.org/privacy/"
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="page-wrap section-space">
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-text-secondary">
      <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl normal-case text-text-primary">
        Privacy and processing
      </h1>
      <p>
        Updated October 2, 2026. This notice describes the current public
        scanner and contact surface.
      </p>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl normal-case text-text-primary mb-4">
          Before submitting text
        </h2>
        <p>
          The public scanner sends your submission to Secure Pride’s
          Cloudflare-hosted API. It does not run entirely on your device or
          within your organization.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Use invented examples or text you are authorized to share. Do not
          submit client records, health information, passwords, or details about
          someone’s identity. Masking happens after the server receives the
          original text.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl normal-case text-text-primary mb-4">
          Scanner processing
        </h2>
        <p>
          The current TypeScript scanner checks text against known patterns. Its
          request handler does not send the text to an external AI model. The
          application does not intentionally save the submitted text to a
          database or include it in its audit log.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Text and results are held in the page’s memory while you use it. Clear
          removes the displayed input and results; it does not delete hosting
          logs or undo a request already received. Copying a redacted draft
          places it on your device’s clipboard, which may sync across devices.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl normal-case text-text-primary mb-4">
          Application audit metadata
        </h2>
        <p>
          Each scan reaching the engine emits a structured log event. It
          includes a trace identifier, timestamp, hashed actor identifier, input
          length, detected data categories, injection severity, and policy
          action. The public interface uses an anonymous actor identifier.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          These events exclude the submitted text, but their categories can
          still reveal sensitive context. A hashed identifier is not a guarantee
          of anonymity.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl normal-case text-text-primary mb-4">
          Hosting details still to verify
        </h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare processes network requests and may handle connection and
          security metadata, such as IP addresses. We have not verified the
          deployment’s log retention, log access, or processing locations for
          this notice. We cannot promise zero hosting logs, a specific
          residency, or a deletion deadline.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          If those details are essential to your work, do not submit sensitive
          information to the hosted scanner. Contact us to discuss the boundary
          first.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl normal-case text-text-primary mb-4">
          Contact and tracking
        </h2>
        <p>
          The public contact links open your email app. Sending a message
          discloses its contents and sender details to the email providers and
          recipient. Include only what is necessary for your question.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The site application does not include an analytics SDK or persist
          scanner text in browser storage. This statement does not cover hosting
          security logs or external sites you choose to visit.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl normal-case text-text-primary mb-4">
          Questions or deletion requests
        </h2>
        <p>
          Email{" "}
          <a class="sp-link" href="mailto:hello@securepride.org">
            hello@securepride.org
          </a>{" "}
          to ask about processing or request deletion of information you
          provided. Do not resend sensitive records as proof of your request.
          What can be located or deleted depends on the information held and the
          hosting configuration.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
